<html>
<title>Disk Support</title>
<body>


<h1>Disk Support</h1>

<p>
Disk support will be activated if the selected XML file includes a disk definition:
</p>
<ul>
<li><code>ide</code>: <code>IDE</code> GUI</li>
<li><code>tu58</code>: <code>TU58</code> GUI</li>
<li><code>wd1770</code>, <code>wd1793</code>: <code>FDC</code> GUI</li>
<li><code>upd765</code>: <code>FDC</code> or <code>HD</code> GUI</li>
</ul>


<h2>FDC GUI</h2>

<p>
<img src="images/disk_fdc.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>FDC x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>File name</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Depending on the configuration, one to four drives (0-3) can be defined. In the example above, a COMX-35 is configured with two <code>WD1770</code> drives. To change a disk at runtime, select a different file name using one of the <strong>FDC x</strong> buttons (1) or type a file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field (2). To eject the disk, use the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3) or remove the file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field.
</p>


<h2>HD GUI</h2>

<p>
<img src="images/disk_hd.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>HD x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Double arrow</strong> button</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Directory</strong> text field</li>
</ul>

<p>
The <code>HD</code> GUI is available for <code>upd765</code> drives; instead of using a disk image, it supports direct access to the host computer hard disk. The HD directory can be specified using the <strong>HD 0</strong> to <strong>HD 3</strong> buttons (1). The directory name will be displayed in the <strong>Directory</strong> text field (3).
</p>

<p>
To switch between <code>HD</code> and <code>FDC</code> mode, press one of the <strong>Double arrow</strong> buttons (2).
</p>

<p>
The <code>HD</code> feature provides direct import/export to and from the host computer file system. Unlike <code>FDC</code> images, which are limited to 310 KB, the <code>HD</code> directory has no total size limit. However, the following per-directory limitations apply:
</p>
<ul>
<li>The maximum number of files in one directory is 128</li>
<li>The maximum file size is 300 KB to 310 KB, depending on how many files are stored in the directory</li>
</ul>


<h2>IDE GUI</h2>

<p>
<img src="images/disk_ide.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>IDE x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>File name</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Two <code>IDE</code> drives (0 and 1) can be defined. In the example above, a COSMAC Elf 2000 is configured. To change a disk at runtime, select a different file name using one of the <strong>IDE x</strong> buttons (1) or type a file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field (2). To eject the disk, use the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3) or remove the file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field.
</p>

<p>
After initial start-up, any file <code>&lt;type&gt;-installation.ide</code> (or <code>&lt;type&gt;-installation.dsk</code>) will be renamed to <code>&lt;type&gt;.ide</code> (or <code>&lt;type&gt;.dsk</code>) if that file does not exist.
</p>


<h2>TU58 GUI</h2>

<p>
<img src="images/disk_tu58.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>TU58 x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>File name</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Two <code>TU58</code> drives (0 and 1) can be defined. In the example above, an SBC1802 is configured. To change a disk at runtime, select a different file name using one of the <strong>TU58 x</strong> buttons (1) or type a file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field (2). To eject the disk, use the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3) or remove the file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field.
</p>

</body>
</html>
